Vikram and Betal: The Foolish King

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the dark forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a king who loved praise,” said Betal. “He liked people who always said good things about him.”

Many courtiers started flattering the king to please him.

But one honest man always spoke the truth, even if it was not pleasing.

The king did not like this and became angry.

One day, the king asked, “Who is the greatest king in the world?”

All the courtiers said, “You are the greatest, Your Majesty!”

But the honest man said, “A truly great king listens to the truth, not just praise.”

The king became angry and ordered him to be punished.

But later, the king thought about his words.

He realized that the honest man was right.

The next day, the king called him back and said, “You are the only one who truly cares about me.”

Betal then asked, “Vikram, who was truly wise?”

Vikram replied, “The honest man was wise because he spoke the truth without fear.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Always value truth over flattery.
